# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# provenance: authored for OdyTTY; synthetic; not derived from upstream sources
# reviewed: yes
# baseline: 24 rows by 80 columns
#
# Absolute and relative cursor addressing.
#
# Escapes: \e ESC, \r CR, \n LF, \t HT, \\ backslash, \xNN one byte.
# Every other character is emitted literally. Lines add no implicit newline.

# Clear the screen and home the cursor so the fixture starts from a known state.
\e[2J\e[H

# Absolute addressing: place a marker at four corners of the baseline grid.
\e[1;1HTL
\e[1;79HTR
\e[24;1HBL
\e[24;79HBR

# Relative movement: from a known origin, walk right, down, left, and up by a
# fixed amount and land back on the origin. A terminal that miscounts any one
# of the four directions leaves the marker somewhere other than row 10.
\e[10;10H
\e[5C\e[3B\e[5D\e[3Aorigin

# Clamping: ask for positions past both edges. The cursor must stop at the last
# row and column rather than wrapping or scrolling.
\e[999;999Hclamp-max
\e[0;0Hclamp-min

# Save and restore. The restored position must be the saved one exactly, and an
# intervening absolute move must not disturb the saved value.
\e[12;40H\e7
\e[1;1H
\e8restored

# Leave the cursor somewhere predictable for the capture.
\e[24;1H
